<title>UK: English Patient, Shine favourites for Oscar.</title>
<headline>English Patient, Shine favourites for Oscar.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>&quot;The English Patient&quot;, nominated in 12 Oscar categories on Tuesday, was named 2-1 joint favourite with &quot;Shine&quot; to win the Best Picture award by British bookmakers Ladbrokes.</p>
<p>Geoffrey Rush, who played the pianist hero of &quot;Shine&quot;, was installed as 6-4 favourite to win the Best Actor award.</p>
<p>Betting prices as follows -</p>
<p>Best Picture -</p>
<p>2-1 &quot;The English Patient&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Shine&quot;</p>
<p>4-1 &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot;</p>
<p>5-1 &quot;Secrets and Lies&quot;</p>
<p>6-1 &quot;Fargo&quot;</p>
<p>Best Actor -</p>
<p>6-4 Geoffrey Rush (Shine)</p>
<p>3-1 Ralph Fiennes (The English Patient)</p>
<p>10-3 Tom Cruise (Jerry Maguire)</p>
<p>11-2 Woody Harrelson (The People vs Larry Flynt)</p>
<p>6-1 Billy Bob Thornton (Slingblade)</p>
<p>Best Actress -</p>
<p>6-4 Brenda Blethyn (Secrets and Lies)</p>
<p>5-2 Diane Keaton (Marvin's Room)</p>
<p>7-2 Kristin Scott Thomas (The English Patient)</p>
<p>6-1 Emily Watson (Breaking the Waves)</p>
<p>Frances McDormand (Fargo)</p>
</text>
